	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85208828391?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {LangChain stands at the intersection of advanced natural language processing and document analysis. LangChain enables users to seamlessly extract information, summarize text, perform searches, answer questions, and even translate content within PDF documents. The exponential growth of digital documents, particularly in Portable Document Format (PDF), necessitates innovative approaches to enhance document interaction and comprehension. The emergence of language models has shown great promise in transforming how individuals engage with textual content. This paper presents a critical review of the "LangChain" model-a novel application of language processing designed to revolutionize interactions with PDF documents. By combining advanced natural language understanding with document analysis, LangChain offers dynamic and intuitive methods for extracting, summarizing, searching, and translating PDF content. Through a comprehensive examination of LangChain's capabilities, architecture, and real-world applications, this review evaluates its potential to address the limitations of conventional PDF readers. Furthermore, this paper assesses LangChain's impact on productivity, accessibility, and collaboration across various domains. By shedding light on the strengths, weaknesses, and future prospects of LangChain, this review contributes to the ongoing discourse on the role of language models in reshaping digital document engagement. © 2024 IEEE.},
