	abstract = {Discovering the person location through a chatbot within the geographical virtual barrier boundary i.e., called Geofence that allows users to detect when someone enters or departs a location. Geofence main motive is for finding the person in a specific area rather than the entire map area. The polygonal geofence is a type of geofence that helps us to cover precisely the boundaries of a building that we want to cover. The coordinates of a building, i.e., the Latitude and Longitude, can be used to generate a polygonal geofence that covers only that area of the building. Although a circular geofence can be utilized, it will cover an undesirable area, which is why a polygonal geofence is preferable. With the assist of GPS/Wi-Fi technology to track a person's location, geofence will cover the necessary geographical virtual barrier borders, and a chatbot will provide the person's location anytime humans ask it. GPS can send location data to the chatbot whether the person is inside the virtual boundary; otherwise, it will indicate that the person is not in that zone. Similarly, Wi-Fi will assist in tracking the location of people inside the building per floor. The chatbot will assist in determining a person's location so that we can determine exactly where the person is standing. The chatbot is a text-based input system that allows us to communicate as if we were chatting with a human. Natural language understanding and Natural Language Generation are used in Natural Language processing the key objective is that any student who desires to meet with a specific teacher to rectify any doubts or submit work can employ this intelligent chatbot to discover the teacher's current position.  © 2022 IEEE.},
