	abstract = {Migration for jobs is a common scenario in rural as well as metro cities. As naïve in kitchen work, people struggle to have good food to maintain their physical health. It is a common practice to do multi-level searches starting from searching the ingredients, then analyzing the quantity, negotiating the prices online/offline, identifying the best recipe etc. Artificial Intelligence has impacted the lifestyles of human beings drastically. A machine can give you a solution to the multi-level searches in one go. Looking at the fast life of people, this paper proposes a novel approach to cart optimization in ecommerce websites or apps by offering selection of ingredients to the quantity decision, negotiating the best prices and the fastest delivery. Our proposed solution will be integrated as an AI assisted approach to assist into dish making by simply thinking of a dish. We propose to integrate Natural Language Processing, collaborative and content-based filtering, ingredient extraction and explainable AI. BERT model will be used to extract ingredients from the video selected by the user and is mapped to inventory products using fuzzy string matching algorithms. DeepIDRS offers personalized recommendations and LIME provides transparent explanations. By leveraging the NLP frameworks for feedback loop, the system is made more user centric and personalized over time. Thus, by bridging the gap between intent recognition, recipe and product recommendation and clear explanations, the system manages to optimize the ecommerce platform by offering an innovative solution. © 2025 IEEE.},
