	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85214642355?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {A chatbot is now a practical tool since it can provide instant, automated, and correct solutions to customer questions. Researchers are using soft computing techniques to make the Chatbot user-friendly, and the methods chosen depend on the complexity of the problem domain. Chatbots have taken over many previously human-only functions, such as the delivery of food, the recommendation of products, the counseling on insurance policies, the assistance with finances, the scheduling of meetings, and many others. However, the potential for chatbots to improve services provided by the public sector has not yet been investigated. The article covers the purposes, difficulties, architecture, and models of AI-powered chatbots. Modern Artificial Intelligence-based systems (AI-Chatbots) and their historical roots in the Turing Test and rule-based systems are examined. This article breaks down the many uses of AI-powered chatbots into two primary categories: services for customers and services for government agencies. The study’s goal is to gain a better understanding of chatbot applications in public service and business support. The survey results show that the AI-powered chatbot system has great potential to enhance government operations and the quality of service provided to the public. © 2024 Scrivener Publishing LLC.},
