	abstract = {Conversational AI has become popular in modern society. This paper discusses one such conversational framework, Continuous Question Answering (CQA), which is designed to support a goal-oriented process. In this paper, an end-to-end intelligent dialogue framework is presented to automate any process in which there is a need to converse by asking questions and evaluating the answers between two entities. The paper discusses the techniques and strategies used to tackle challenges in the areas of Natural Language Understanding, Contextual Modeling, Dialogue Planning, Question Generation, and Information Retrieval. To demonstrate the efficiency of the CQA framework, an end-to-end recruitment system is developed to interview candidates and grade them accordingly. The system understands the user’s prior knowledge and intelligently sets up an open-ended interview process. The goal of the system is to assess the user’s technical proficiency through a Question-and-Answer framework and recommend the best candidates to the employer for a specific job role. A grading system is used to evaluate each candidate and provide an in-depth analysis of their performance. The system received a human satisfaction score of 4.3 out of 5 for the recruitment system implemented using the CQA framework, which outperforms other state-of-the-art conversational systems. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Dr. Vivek Sunnapwar, Dr. Hariram Chavan and Dr. Namrata F. Ansari; individual chapters, the contributors.},
