	abstract = {The modern world faces a crucial mental health problem because substantial populations worldwide experience anxiety and depression and stress-related conditions. People face several obstacles when accessing prompt and quality mental healthcare, including service distribution limitations together with cost barriers and social discrimination against treatment needs. The integration of artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) technology gave rise to ChatBots that serve as promising tools to link users with mental health assistance. A knowledgeable ChatBot system represents the main objective to build a mental health assistance platform. Users engage with the ChatBot through natural language processing technology which allows effective understanding of their inquiries and offers responses that convey empathy. The empathetic user-interaction stands critical when supporting mental health because users experience genuine understanding and compassionate care which builds better conversational outcomes. The ChatBot uses a wide range of mental health discussions for training to detect emotional signals while sorting through user queries and recommending helpful resources including coping techniques and breathing techniques and mental health support lines. The learning framework evolves based on user interaction and feedback to increase both the appropriate match and personalized delivery of responses progressively. The chapter highlights the technological innovations that have made the ChatBot possible, but it also stresses the necessity of developing a user-friendly and accessible tool that puts its users’ welfare first. The sentiment analysis algorithms combined with intent recognition enabled by machine learning within the ChatBot system produce conversations which help users handle their mental health needs efficiently. This chapter proves how AI and ML systems bring mental health assistance, which provides a scalable accessible solution alongside compassionate interaction to users who need help. © 2026 Scrivener Publishing LLC.},
