	abstract = {In academic settings, both students and faculty often find themselves facing the same questions over and over again about schedules, exams, and administrative processes. This can lead to delays in communication and put extra pressure on staff. To tackle this issue, we've created InfoMate, a smart conversational system designed to automate the resolution of academic queries using Natural Language Processing (NLP). The system understands user questions in everyday language, breaks them down through tokenization and intent detection with tools like NLTK and spaCy, and pulls relevant answers from a structured MySQL database via a Flask-based backend. The chatbot delivers quick responses about academic schedules, exam dates, and departmental announcements through both text and voice. In tests, it achieved an impressive average accuracy of 89.3% and a response time of just 1.9 seconds, proving it can handle queries efficiently and reliably. This system not only makes information more accessible but also lightens the workload for staff, paving the way for smarter academic assistance frameworks. Our work showcases how feasible and scalable lightweight NLP-driven chatbots can be in higher education.  © 2025 IEEE.},
